# Adjudicated punused findings. CI runs punused per directory and matches each
# finding line against the literal substrings below: an unmatched finding fails
# the build, an unmatched entry warns as stale. Entries name the symbol, never
# file:line:col, and the "#" lines above each entry carry its reason.

# punused drives gopls, whose reference view cannot see a method that
# encoding/json or encoding/xml calls through reflection, nor a struct field
# that only a decoder and an encoder touch. Every entry below is one of those.

# Called by xml.Unmarshal(body, l) in animelists.Parse: the whole Anime-Lists
# decode runs through it. Deleting it fails the cmd/animap build tests.
method (*listXML).UnmarshalXML is unused

# The compact [season, episode, absolute, air date] form of captured.tvdb
# episodes in every committed overlay and bridge file. Decoded by
# overlay.ReadEntry, encoded by `animap overlay capture` and overlay.SetHash.
# Deleting either fails TestEpisodeJSONRoundTrip and the cmd/animap build tests.
method (Episode).MarshalJSON is unused
method (*Episode).UnmarshalJSON is unused

# The anilist_ids key of the overlay file format (docs/overlay.md), present in
# every committed overlay/*.json. overlay.ReadEntry refuses unknown keys, so
# without the field every entry fails to load, and overlay.SetHash marshals it
# into the published sources.overlay.sha256.
field AniListIDs is unused
